```css
:root {
  --mainLightRed: rgba(208, 101, 153, 1); /* Light red leanning slightly towards pink */
}

/* Darkened variation by 15% */
:root {
  --dMainLightRed: darken(var(--mainLightRed), 15%);
}
```

These custom properties can be used throughout your stylesheet as needed, to maintain consistency with the base color and its darkened variation. Adjust the RGB values of `--mainLightRed` as necessary to better approximate the desired light red with a medium light shade of pink. Note, for an exact match consider examining the font's built-in colors or Material Design Palette extensions.
